Here's how to handle each scenario in MSTest:

**1. Windows-only tests — use `[TestCategory]` + conditional skip or `#if`:**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("WindowsOnly")]
[Ignore("Requires Windows Registry - skipped on non-Windows")]
// Or at runtime:
public void RegistryTest()
{
    if (!OperatingSystem.IsWindows())
        Assert.Inconclusive("Requires Windows");
    // ... test logic
}
```

**2. Skip in CI (requires local GPU):**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[TestCategory("RequiresGPU")]
public void GpuTest()
{
    if (Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable("CI") == "true")
        Assert.Inconclusive("Skipped in CI - requires local GPU");
    // ... test logic
}
```

**3. Flaky external API — use `[Retry]` (MSTest v3+):**

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)] // Retries up to 3 times on failure
[TestCategory("Flaky")]
public void WeatherApiTest()
{
    var result = CallWeatherApi();
    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
}
```

**4. Cleanup even on failure — use `[TestCleanup]` or `try/finally`:**

```csharp
private string? _tempFile;

[TestInitialize]
public void Setup()
{
    _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
}

[TestCleanup]
public void Cleanup()
{
    if (_tempFile != null && File.Exists(_tempFile))
        File.Delete(_tempFile);
}

[TestMethod]
public void FileProcessingTest()
{
    File.WriteAllText(_tempFile!, "test data");
    // ... assertions — Cleanup runs even if this throws
}
```

**Filtering at run time:**

```bash
# Exclude flaky + GPU tests in CI
dotnet test --filter "TestCategory!=Flaky&TestCategory!=RequiresGPU"
```

**Key takeaways:**
| Scenario | Mechanism |
|----------|-----------|
| Platform-specific | `Assert.Inconclusive()` / `OperatingSystem.IsWindows()` |
| CI skip | Check env var + `Assert.Inconclusive()` |
| Flaky retry | `[Retry(N)]` attribute (MSTest v3+) |
| Guaranteed cleanup | `[TestCleanup]` method |
